A strip of controls with a single tab stop - the arrow keys move between them.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/toolbar)

<%= embed AppicaUI::ToolbarPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Toolbar(aria_label: "Formatting") do
  ToolbarGroup(aria_label: "Text style") do
    ToolbarButton { |item| Button(**item, variant: :ghost) { "Bold" } }
    ToolbarButton { |item| Button(**item, variant: :ghost) { "Italic" } }
  end
  ToolbarSeparator()
  ToolbarLink(href: "#help") { "Help" }
end
```

Items are composed, not styled: `ToolbarButton`, `ToolbarLink` and `ToolbarInput` hand their attributes to the
control you give them - a [Button](<%= page_path(:button) %>), a [Toggle](<%= page_path(:toggle) %>), a
[SelectTrigger](<%= page_path(:select) %>), an [Input](<%= page_path(:input) %>) - so it keeps its look and joins the
roving focus. A toolbar never wraps: when there's no room it scrolls along its axis (scrollbar hidden).

